  "description": "Atom binding via the canonical Jones-Markov trace (Direction 1 of validity audit): matches the prop's explicit-values table tr_M(σ_0)=z, tr_M(σ_0σ_1)=z², tr_M(σ_0σ_1σ_0)=hz²+z. Replaces the Plancherel-weighted trace used in binding_3A and atom_markov_trace. Binding = Q_β(n)·(tr_M_free − tr_M_atom) [SIGNED categorical difference; the double-modulus |·|−|·| was a non-archimedean misuse] with Q_β(n) = 0.78233341 MeV (free-neutron β-decay Q-value, the CAL-2 proxy — NOT CAL-3, which is P_avg^π; Q_β is a scored prediction, not an input — NOT the canonical E_0 = m_e/(q_0(q_0-1)) ≈ 4.186 MeV). DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: predicted B values are 5–40× smaller than AME because Q_β is the wrong energy scale; the primary canonical mass-prediction pipeline is canonical-mass-table-extended.witness.json. This witness is retained for the Direction 1 validity audit of the Jones-Markov trace itself.",
