    "precision_note": "Two different precisions, kept apart. ARITHMETIC: Q_beta_n_MeV is the exact decimal M_N - M_P - M_E of the quoted CODATA-2022 / AME inputs; B_MeV = Q_beta_n_MeV * delta_tr is that decimal times the 50-dps trace difference, serialized at 50 significant digits, every one determined by those inputs. B_AME_MeV is the AME2020 table's own decimal text, verbatim. delta_m_over_m_pct is computed from these and serialized at 50 digits. EXPERIMENT: Q_beta(n) carries a CODATA uncertainty of 6.664e-07 MeV (8.518e-07 relative), so B_MeV as a PHYSICAL prediction is meaningful only to ~6 significant figures; the extra digits are not a claim of measurement, they are what the arithmetic gives for the quoted inputs. Q_beta cancels in any ratio B(a)/B(b) = delta_tr(a)/delta_tr(b), so ratio consumers should read delta_tr_exact, which has no experimental input at all."
